TI  - Arbuscular mycorrhizal inoculation increases maize grain yield in low-phosphorus soils of central Mexico
PY  - 2019
T2  - Journal of Field Agronomy
VL  - 41
IS  - 3
SP  - 211
EP  - 224
AB  - We evaluated the effect of inoculation with arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi on maize under field conditions. Inoculated plots were compared with non-inoculated controls in a randomized complete block design with four replicates. Grain yield increased by 9% on average, and the response was larger where available soil phosphorus was low.
